{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794347475,"nonce":"YRYHdHALOqrceDraVMd1Rldqf9Q=","message":"Coverage, continued (unit.hl, 8688 functions):\n\n- b160fd5d array sizes and raw memory (ArraySize, MemGet/MemSet): 44.3%\n- 955fc743 closures (StaticClosure, InstanceClosure): 57.5%. A static closure is allocated per execution here; LLVM emits one constant object.\n- aee2fa43 casts (ToVirtual, UnsafeCast, ToDyn, SafeCast unbox/box/copy) and local sharing: 76.6% (6657)\n\nEach step: unit conformance with ASH_WASM_DIRECT=1 is 1069/1069 cases and 10971/10971 assertions on both the wasm and wasm-fibers arms; clippy clean in the four CI configurations plus wasm32.\n\nFinding from the casts step: the first run of the wasm-fibers arm timed out listing cases. The module had gone to 26 MB (plain 16.5 MB) because every AIR value had its own wasm local: one function had 8528 locals, another 3715, where LLVM's equivalents have 10 to 20. The fiber transform spills per local, so those bodies grew 2.6x, and cranelift's compile time grows faster than linearly with them. aee2fa43 adds a local allocator (crates/ash_wasm_emit/src/locals.rs): interference from AIR liveness, greedy colouring per wasm type. Those two functions now have 18 and 56 locals; linked code is 11.53 MB plain and 19.96 MB with fibers (was 11.81 and 21.56). The fibers module is still 1.73x the plain one in code bytes.\n\nThe machine was heavily loaded by other work throughout (load average 40 to 190), so no compile-time or launch-time figure from this session is usable. Both need to be measured on the NUC: LLVM vs direct build time, and wasmtime/browser compile time of the resulting module, with and without fibers.\n\nStill declined, by first blocker: casts that need the value in memory (dyn_cast* take a pointer to the value; needs by-value runtime wrappers) 309, CallClosure 303, CallMethod 203, exceptions and trap regions 191, CellSet 176, EnumField 138.","files":null}]}